[00:00.00] Oh, those yellow creek waters,
[00:15.00] They the sons and daughters of an Indian nation
[00:21.00] Called the Cherokee
[00:24.00] Then came those pioneer settlers
[00:28.00] That drove the Indians westward
[00:31.00] Far from their homes
[00:34.00] Down on Yellow Creek
[00:37.00] Now it's many years later
[00:41.00] I'm living into nature
[00:44.00] In this Indian paradise
[00:48.00] Called Tennessee
[00:51.00] Where I find those broken arrows
[00:55.00] That blew like the sparrows
[00:58.00] The sparrows that still fly
[01:01.00] Down on Yellow Creek
